  "status_text": "One table can decide whether a single small circuit can make all the lights blink on cue. Give it a finite list of switch settings and limits on gates and bit flips. Start with the input wire patterns and both constants. Each step adds a new pattern from a legal gate, and the table keeps the fewest bit flips for each collection. Lean checked that an entry within the limits contains all the requested patterns exactly when one circuit can realize them together within those limits (L-lib-1336). A covering table can also certify exclusions (L-lib-1335).",
